where_rounded.plain, line 2: Add brackets to show what "rounded to 2 places" goes with.

    show the total of amounts where it is more than 100 rounded to 2 places
         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Try one of these:
    show (the total of amounts where it is more than 100) rounded to 2 places
  or
    show the total of amounts where it is more than (100 rounded to 2 places)
Why: "rounded to 2 places" could go with everything before it, or only with "100" at the end of the "where" check. Plain never guesses which one you mean.

where_rounded.plain, line 4: Add brackets to show what "joined with" goes with.

    show names where it starts with "a" joined with ", "
         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Try one of these:
    show (names where it starts with "a") joined with ", "
  or
    show names where it starts with ("a" joined with ", ")
Why: "joined with" could go with everything before it, or only with "a" at the end of the "where" check. Plain never guesses which one you mean.

